Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/pgssubdec: clear a palette's CLUT when its epoch restarts

A PGS palette segment is only a delta while the display set carrying it is
Normal state. At an acquisition point or an epoch start the segment replaces
the palette: every entry it does not carry is transparent. libbluray, which
implements the disc spec, spells that out in graphics_processor.c's
_decode_pds -- state 0 calls pg_decode_palette_update, anything else calls
pg_decode_palette, which memsets the entry table before applying the segment
(clause 8.8.3.1.1).

pgssubdec releases the epoch in flush_cache(), but flush_cache() only zeroes
palettes.count; PGSSubPalette.clut keeps its contents, and the next epoch's
first palette segment reuses that same slot and writes only the entries it
carries. Everything else silently inherits the previous epoch's colours.

The visible failure is a caption whose bitmap background index is not among
the entries the new palette carries: it renders in whatever colour an earlier
caption left at that index, so the subtitles sit in an opaque box whose shade
changes from caption to caption -- black, grey, or the same white as the text.
Reported against Plezy as a forced PGS track on a UHD remux (edde746/plezy#2391);
media3's decoder hides it only because it zeroes all 256 entries on every
palette segment, which is wrong for the delta case.

Clear the CLUT where the slot is handed out. Within an epoch find_palette()
returns the palette that already exists, so Normal-state delta updates keep
inheriting entries exactly as before; only a slot re-issued after a flush
starts transparent.

Verified against the pinned n8.0.1: a retail 208-display-set forced PGS track
renders byte-identically across 1500 frames before and after, while a stream
whose second display set is an acquisition point or an epoch start loses the
phantom box and a Normal-state delta keeps its authored one. Not upstream yet;
drop this patch once the pinned FFmpeg clears the CLUT itself.

diff --git a/libavcodec/pgssubdec.c b/libavcodec/pgssubdec.c
index 20583c9..d5789e5 100644
--- a/libavcodec/pgssubdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/pgssubdec.c
@@ -346,6 +346,10 @@ static int parse_palette_segment(AVCodecContext *avctx,
         }
         palette = &ctx->palettes.palette[ctx->palettes.count++];
         palette->id  = id;
+        /* flush_cache() only drops the count, so this slot can still hold the
+         * previous epoch's CLUT. Every entry a new epoch does not define is
+         * fully transparent. */
+        memset(palette->clut, 0, sizeof(palette->clut));
     }
 
     /* Skip palette version */
